@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB Localization
	Frontend testing for creating an osb localization

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I sign out and sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	* I tear down the localizations with the folowing keys and values
	| $1 billion - $10 billion | $1 billion - $10 billion |

Scenario: Add Localization
	Admins should be able to add a localization on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "OSB Localization" portlet under the "Content & Data" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I create a localization with the key "$1 billion - $10 billion" and value "$1 billion - $10 billion"
	Then I should be able to view a localization with the key "$1 billion - $10 billion" and value "$1 billion - $10 billion" in the position "1"